# A regular hexagon made in the shape editor without typing TOML. The editor's box is 80×40
# cells from row 3, column 9 (a square in world units). Six clicks place the vertices, a cell or
# so off where a regular hexagon's corners are: the guides snap the second to 0°, the third to
# 60° and the first side's length, and the rest to the next corner of a regular polygon; the
# last click, on the first vertex, closes it. Dragging the top side's middle up bends it into a
# curve. N renames the path, n names a vertex, a names the area inside by clicking it, i gives
# the shape its id and input, w says what the region shows, b binds the preview to two volcanoes.
# tests/drive.rs reads the saved .cold-lava/shapes.toml after and renders it.
size 140x44
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter
type Editor
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Editor
keys S
wait-for shape editor · type to filter
type new
keys enter
wait-for shape editor · shape1 (new) · vertices
click 10 34
click 10 64
wait-for ⊹ 0°
click 23 79
wait-for ⊹ 60° · = side
click 36 64
wait-for ⊹ regular: same side, same angle
click 36 34
click 23 19
click 10 34
wait-for closed path of 6 vertices
expect path1: path, 6 vertices, closed
expect-in 10 34 10 34 ●
expect-in 36 64 36 64 ●
keys v
drag 10 49 6 49
wait-for path1: path, 6 vertices, 1 curved, closed
expect-in 6 49 6 49 ◦
keys N
wait-for rename the part
keys backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace
type hex
keys enter
wait-for hex: path
keys n
click 10 64
wait-for name the anchor
type corner
keys enter
wait-for anchor hex.corner
keys a
click 23 49
wait-for in hex: hex
type inside
keys enter
wait-for inside = hex
keys i
wait-for the shape
keys backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace
type hexagon
keys tab
type Hexagon
keys tab
type items
keys enter
wait-for inputs: items
keys w
wait-for what each region shows
type items
keys enter
wait-for shows items
keys b
wait-for preview data
type items:Fuji, Krakatoa
keys enter
wait-for preview · bound
expect-in 26 97 43 140 Krakatoa
keys ctrl+s
wait-for saved hexagon in .cold-lava/shapes.toml
screen
keys q
wait-for whiteboard Editor
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
